 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Finite refinements of blow-ups",
 "statement": "Let $T$ be qcqs and $U\\subseteq T$ a quasi-compact open. Finitely many\n$U$-admissible blow-ups of $T$ ([sk-def-nagata-admissible]) admit a common\n$U$-admissible blow-up. A composite of two $U$-admissible blow-ups is again\nsuch a blow-up. A $U$-admissible blow-up on a quasi-compact open\n$V\\subseteq T$ containing $U$ extends to a $U$-admissible blow-up of $T$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-lem-nagata-sketch-blowups/_section.md",
  "place": "node sk-lem-nagata-sketch-blowups, order 10"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "sk-def-nagata-admissible",
  "sk-def-nagata-sketch-data"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "For ideals $\\mathcal I,\\mathcal J$, blowing up their product factors through\nboth blow-ups. Indeed, after the product becomes an invertible ideal, each\nfactor is invertible, and the universal property applies. More explicitly,\nfirst blowing up $\\mathcal I$ and then the pulled-back $\\mathcal J$ gives the\nblow-up of $\\mathcal I\\mathcal J$ (Stacks 080A). Induction proves the first\nassertion. For a center on the first blow-up which is not itself pulled back\nfrom $T$, the composition assertion is the finite-type ideal calculation in\nStacks 080B.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  },
  {
   "text": "The extension assertion uses extension of finite-type quasi-coherent ideals\nfrom a quasi-compact open, with a center still outside $U$; the precise\nadmissible extension result is Stacks 080M. These two results turn finitely\nmany local constructions into one global modification preserving $U$.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
